         13,
         6
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Solve each equation for x: \\( x = 4 y^{2} \\) from the graph of h, with \\( y \\ge 0 \\), and \\( x = y + 3 \\) from the graph of k.",
         "rule_named": "rewrite each curve as a function of y"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The curves meet where \\( 4 y^{2} = y + 3 \\), at \\( y = 1 \\), and the region runs from the x-axis, \\( y = 0 \\), up to there. On that interval the line is to the right of the parabola.",
         "rule_named": "limits in y and the right-hand curve"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The area is \\( \\int_{0}^{1} \\left(\\left(y + 3\\right) - \\left(4 y^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,dy = \\frac{13}{6} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            13,
            6
         ],
         "rule_named": "area integral in y"
      }
   ],
